Z||000009||FLASHY||06-27-2001||11:30 PM||||What I can't stand is seeing these young punks drive by with their seats pushed as far back as possible and reclined WAY back and then they have to RRRRREEEEEAAAAAACCCCCCCHHHHHHHH so far in front of them to hang onto the steering wheel. Not to mention the 6" lifts on their shoes so they can reach the gas pedal. They must do that so if their buddy wants to try sitting in their seat they'll feel small.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/flashy_sig.gif"> <P>"I know you believe you understand what you think I wrote, but I'm not sure you realize that what you read is not what I really meant"||||reg||8
Z||000010||Songman||06-27-2001||11:32 PM||||Because we can.....<P>Actually, I can see a lot of reasons for it.. Being that I am not perfect and don't always keep my hands perfectly on the wheel, and always at 10 and 2...<P>Sometimes it could be because I had to do something to my car and don't want to get grease on my steering wheel.<P>Sometimes it could be because I am holding a 44 ounce Big Gulp in my hand.<P>It makes it easier to wave at everybody as they pass. (A Southern thing)<P>Sometimes the steering wheel is hot.<P>And God forbid, sometimes we do it just because it feels good. <P>Of course, if someone had given me the "How To Correctly Hold Your Steering Wheel" handbook, I probably wouldn't be guilty of such heinous crimes as this...<P>And to make matters worse, I do it in the Fieros, I do it in the Lexus, I do it in the Monte Carlo... I even do it in the Navigator! <P>I better go turn myself in to the authorities... heheh<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 06-27-2001).]||||reg||12
