Z||000037||Ken Wittlief||06-29-2001||02:01 PM||||Using your a$$ for an airbag works on the opposite theory - the gas is already in it all the time, and when you hit all the gas is expelled into the passenger cabin.<P>  Like regular airbags this is also bad for people with ashma - they can have serious adverse reactions.<P>  And if you are sitting up againts the assbag when it 'goes off' it is fatal almost 100% of the time - you need to stay 10" or more away from it.<P>  as for driving with your wrist?! maybe they are afraid to grip the wheel firmly incase of unexpected airbag inflation?<P>  I think the reason kids put their seats all the way back, and then lean them all the way back, is cause they have an overinflated image of how tall they are: "Im so tall I have to put the seat in my car all the way back"<P>  I read somewhere from a race driver the best seat location is when you put both shoulders against the seat and reach straight out with your arms, your wrists should be on the wheel - if your seat is back too far then you have no leverage to turn the wheel hard if you need to - like if a tire blows out.<P>   maybe thats what these guys are doing - constantly checking to see if there seatback is in the right position, by putting their wrists on the steering wheel.<P> or maybe they read the same article and didnt understand it - and think race car drivers DRIVE like this?!||||reg||1
